1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,816
How does a buyer reach the bank's payment page, and nobody else?

2
00:00:03,866 --> 00:00:10,656
A hotel key card opens one room, only for the guest who holds it, and only until checkout.

3
00:00:10,706 --> 00:00:12,672
The payment page works the same way.

4
00:00:12,722 --> 00:00:15,984
The merchant sends the buyer a link with a one-time key.

5
00:00:16,034 --> 00:00:20,232
The bank keeps only a fingerprint of that key, and the link expires.

6
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:24,384
The page shows the website, the amount, and the cards it accepts.

7
00:00:24,434 --> 00:00:28,944
It opens a card-entry session with the card zone and puts the card frame inside.

8
00:00:28,994 --> 00:00:33,504
The page listens only to the frame, and accepts only a token from it.

9
00:00:33,554 --> 00:00:38,040
ecom checks the card belongs to this payment, and then the charge starts.

10
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:43,296
And a double click never runs twice: one lock lets only one step through at a time.

11
00:00:43,346 --> 00:00:45,408
Next: the charge itself.
